<title>CANADA: Canadian West Coast Vessel Loadings - CWB.</title>
<headline>Canadian West Coast Vessel Loadings - CWB.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Wheat Board  reported six ships loading, 13 waiting and eight due at the Canadian West Coast, as of Tuesday.</p>
<p>The longest wait to load on the West Coast was 13 days. Seven ship loaded in Thunder Bay, one waited and five were due. One ships loaded in Baie Comeau, one in Quebec City and one in Port Cartier while nine ships were due on the East Coast.</p>
<p>    Port	 Loading	Waiting</p>
<p>    Vancouver	 5	     7</p>
<p>    Prince Rupert   1	     6</p>
<p>--Gilbert Le Gras 204-947-3548</p>
